  "worked_solution": "First, notice that we are given that \n\n$$\n{T}^{-1}:[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]\u27f6[\\begin{aligned}3x+{y}^{2} \\\\ y\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nSubstituting $3x+{y}^{2}=u$ and $y=v$ into the equation of the first curve, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(3x+{y}^{2})^{2}+y=5\\,\u27f9\\,{u}^{2}+v=5\\,\u27f9\\,v=5-{u}^{2},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhile substituting $y=v$ into the equation of the second curve, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y=0\\,\u27f9\\,v=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find the intersections of the curves in the $uv$-plane, we solve the following system:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}v=5-{u}^{2} \\\\ v=0\\end{aligned}\\,\u27f9\\,{\\begin{aligned}u=\\pm \\sqrt{5} \\\\ v=0.\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the intersection points are $(\\pm \\sqrt{5},0).$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14073263/assets/f667b68a08f6897af0116778f5f21c5b8b0d1ce6aff09e315431dc445d6998bb.png)\n\nAs a result, our domain in the $uv$-plane has the type I representation \n\n$$\n{T}^{-1}(D)={(u,v)\\,:\\,-\\sqrt{5}\\le u\\le \\sqrt{5},\\,0\\le v\\le 5-{u}^{2}}.\n$$",
